{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_40g13lYyOv8vjhkUeTxfLQ5r","content":"1\t# BL-HOST-PREFLIGHT-OBSERVABILITY (supporting diagnosis only)\n2\t\n3\t## Scope and evidence\n4\t\n5\tThis section 1.5 supporting task does not replace the active release batch or\n6\tchange progress.json/features.json. The Coordinator uses the null-binding\n7\tPlanner compatibility path. Product changes require an isolated Generator,\n8\tpre/post scope review and a fresh Kimi-family supporting Evaluator.\n9\t\n10\tBase: 1f52c86d5e5448ed48959cb1bfe63b6de1d26798. Product/script/workflow baseline:\n11\t76d916ba2e3a7147acda5ac9ef15fa70a9cd9958.\n12\t\n13\tApproved run 37812774615 returned a valid redacted refusal at compose_unavailable:\n14\tDocker server 29.1.3, Linux/x86_64, before any configuration/app/DB identity\n15\tchecks. The SSH command uses env -i without HOME. This does not prove that HOME\n16\tor plugin discovery caused the refusal. Do not install or repair anything on\n17\tthe host based on this hypothesis.\n18\t\n19\t## Allowed edits\n20\t\n21\t- scripts/ci/vps-host-preflight.sh: fixed redacted metadata for the existing\n22\t  Compose version query and report serialization only.\n23\t- .github/workflows/deploy-vps.yml: extend only the existing host-preflight jq\n24\t  report validator with exact metadata keys/types/enums. Every byte outside\n25\t  that validator is frozen, including all release jobs and SSH invocation.\n26\t- New tests/ci/vps-host-preflight-observability.test.ts, this spec and new\n27\t  docs/test-reports/BL-HOST-PREFLIGHT-OBSERVABILITY-20261009/ artifacts.\n28\t\n29\tAll existing tests/fixtures/assertions/skips/timeouts, product source, dependencies,\n30\tDB schema, canonical batch state, rules, credentials and previous evidence are\n31\tfrozen. The shared query() implementation and all non-Compose queries are frozen.\n32\tWorkers must not push, use GH production APIs/SSH, alter Secrets/environments,\n33\tinstall host tools, or access production/user queues and credential stores.\n34\t\n35\t## Fixed report contract\n36\t\n37\tKeep schema_version=1 and all old outcome/reason/fields and acceptance rules.\n38\tAdd a required compose_probe object to full reports with exactly:\n39\t\n40\t- status: not_run, ok, command_failed, invalid_version, output_bound_exceeded.\n41\t- pipeline_exit_status: null before execution, otherwise an integer 0..255\n42\t  representing the existing bounded capture pipeline's exit status. Name and\n43\t  documentation must not pretend this is necessarily Docker's own exit code.\n44\t- captured_bytes: null before execution, otherwise an integer 0..16385 for\n45\t  the bounded captured shell string, excluding stripped trailing newlines.\n46\t  Never claim this measures total stdout or stderr emitted by the command.\n47\t- home_present: Boolean presence of the HOME variable, not its value, path,\n48\t  existence/accessibility, emptiness, or whether any Docker config was read.\n49\t\n50\tThe existing missing-jq minimal refusal remains unchanged and is not a valid\n51\tfull transport report. Before the Compose query status is not_run with null\n52\tmetrics. On valid semver and successful capture it is ok. Nonzero capture fails\n53\tclosed as command_failed unless the existing output cap is exceeded; successful\n54\tcapture with an invalid semver is invalid_version. An exceeded cap has status\n55\toutput_bound_exceeded. Every such refusal retains reason=compose_unavailable,\n56\tversions.compose=unknown, outcome=refused and stops at the same branch.\n57\t\n58\tExit 124/137/141 is recorded as a number, not proof of a timeout, owned-tree\n59\tcleanup, a missing plugin, or a particular internal cause. No timeout inference\n60\tor fallback-success behavior is allowed. The existing 5s/16384-byte query bound,\n61\t16385-byte cap detector, 150s SSH/65536-byte report bounds stay unchanged.\n62\t\n63\tNo raw invalid version text, stdout/stderr, HOME/path/config contents, secret\n64\tvalues/hashes or additional environment fields may be emitted by the new metadata.\n65\tThe existing approved files.* metadata/hash allowlist is byte-frozen; do not remove\n66\tor expand it. Tag supporting implementation commits BL-RELEASE-READINESS-F003;\n67\tthis supporting name does not create a canonical feature or change F003 status.\n68\tDo not restore\n69\tHOME, inherit environment, query plugin directories, invoke fallback binaries,\n70\tchange Docker context/config, add host queries or perform host writes.\n71\t\n72\t## Acceptance and publication\n73\t\n74\tPreserve and execute every existing host-preflight test unchanged. Add synthetic\n75\tcontrols for valid version, command failure, invalid/canary output, oversized\n76\toutput, bounded hung query, unset HOME and set HOME with a path canary; prove\n77\tunchanged query argv, no added/mutation queries and no later queries on refusal.\n78\tExercise the real workflow validator: reject missing/extra metadata keys, bad\n79\tstatus/type/range/null metrics and secret-bearing report additions. Pin the\n80\tunchanged workflow body outside the validator and shared/non-Compose script\n81\tbehavior against the base. Do not weaken failures or use retries to green.\n82\t\n83\tSupporting acceptance is local/synthetic only, not parent F004/F005, native\n84\tWindows acceptance, backup/recovery, predecessor identity, or release signoff.\n85\trelease_ready remains false. All raw initial failures must be retained.\n86\t\n87\tOnly the Coordinator may publish an exact reviewed/evaluated commit to a safe\n88\tnon-main branch and dispatch operation=host-preflight. The new run must still\n89\trequire actual protected human production review. All normal verification,\n90\tOCI/recovery and Deploy jobs must be skipped for that operation. No main push,\n91\tservice/config/DB mutation, installation or bootstrap is authorized by this task."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_I0hhqwiANXWGIC43S1m1p3wc","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n3\t  \"title\": \"verdict-artifact\",\n4\t  \"description\": \"autonomous-mode.md 机件 #3 的验收工件 schema。verify 每轮必产 docs/test-reports/{BL-id}-verdict.json，喂沉淀引擎（§8.4）。存在≠真实：每 feature 的 evidence / steps_to_reproduce 必须非空，机械拒收空壳 PASS。v1.1 起兼作 dispatch-mode.md 的跨厂商交付契约（deliverable.schema），并承载 waiting 中断态。\",\n5\t  \"type\": \"object\",\n6\t  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n7\t  \"required\": [\"batch_id\", \"fix_round\", \"created_at\", \"verdicts\"],\n8\t  \"properties\": {\n9\t    \"batch_id\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"= progress.json.current_sprint（BL-id）\" },\n10\t    \"fix_round\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 0 },\n11\t    \"created_at\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n12\t    \"waiting\": {\n13\t      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"],\n14\t      \"enum\": [\"auth\", \"adjudication\", null],\n15\t      \"default\": null,\n16\t      \"description\": \"dispatch-mode.md 的中断态降维表达（借 A2A AUTH_REQUIRED / INPUT_REQUIRED 语义）。一次性 CLI 进程无法「挂起等你」，故把中断态编码进产物：撞 L2 边界而未获授权 → 'auth'；规格歧义 / acceptance 无法客观判定 → 'adjudication'。写完照常 exit 0——不要用非零退出码表达「我需要人」，那会被回执推断判成 FAILED 并触发无意义重派。编排者读到非空即硬停交人类。\"\n17\t    },\n18\t    \"waiting_detail\": {\n19\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n20\t      \"minLength\": 1,\n21\t      \"description\": \"waiting 非空时必填：卡在哪条 feature、需要什么授权或裁决。人类据此一眼判断如何解锁\"\n22\t    },\n23\t    \"verdicts\": {\n24\t      \"type\": \"array\",\n25\t      \"items\": {\n26\t        \"type\": \"object\",\n27\t        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n28\t        \"required\": [\"feature_id\", \"result\", \"evidence\", \"steps_to_reproduce\"],\n29\t        \"properties\": {\n30\t          \"feature_id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n31\t          \"result\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"PASS\", \"PARTIAL\", \"FAIL\"] },\n32\t          \"evidence\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"description\": \"实测证据（测试输出/命令/staging 结果），非空——空 = 空壳，拒收\" },\n33\t          \"steps_to_reproduce\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1 }\n34\t        }\n35\t      }\n36\t    }\n37\t  },\n38\t  \"if\": {\n39\t    \"properties\": { \"waiting\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"auth\", \"adjudication\"] } },\n40\t    \"required\": [\"waiting\"]\n41\t  },\n42\t  \"then\": {\n43\t    \"_comment\": \"中断态下允许 verdicts 为空或部分——被授权/裁决卡住时本就验不完，强行要求满额会逼出编造的证据\",\n44\t    \"required\": [\"waiting_detail\"],\n45\t    \"properties\": { \"verdicts\": { \"minItems\": 0 } }\n46\t  },\n47\t  \"else\": {\n48\t    \"_comment\": \"非中断态：verdicts 必须非空，否则这轮验收没有产出，沉淀引擎无燃料\",\n49\t    \"properties\": { \"verdicts\": { \"minItems\": 1 } }\n50\t  }\n51\t}"}
{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_jkDKddVxboEdfBo4RR8fH9E5","function":{"name":"Read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"scripts/ci/vps-host-preflight.sh\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_Ob0gShqFAWQvPNpEvwsKUbHi","function":{"name":"Read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"tests/ci/vps-host-preflight-observability.test.ts\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_hpgK1TMiFdsXqHaTzXGMlSNK","function":{"name":"Bash","arguments":"{\"command\":\"df -h /Volumes/ORICO/project/.hpoke-20261009 2>&1; ls /Volumes/ORICO/project/.hpoke-20261009 2>&1; ls tests/ci/ | head -30\"}"}}]}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_Ob0gShqFAWQvPNpEvwsKUbHi","content":"1\timport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\n2\timport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\n3\timport { chmodSync, existsSync, mkdirSync, mkdtempSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, rmSync, statSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n4\timport { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\n5\timport { join } from 'node:path';\n6\timport { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\n7\t\n8\tconst base = 'a5ea6e3f66ab4b4b831de88a6bcb078f444b2aca';\n9\tconst sha = 'c'.repeat(40);\n10\tconst scriptPath = 'scripts/ci/vps-host-preflight.sh';\n11\tconst workflowPath = '.github/workflows/deploy-vps.yml';\n12\tconst script = readFileSync(scriptPath, 'utf8');\n13\tconst workflow = readFileSync(workflowPath, 'utf8');\n14\tconst secret = 'SECRET_OUTPUT_CANARY_NEVER_RETAIN';\n15\tconst homeCanary = '/synthetic/HOME_PATH_CANARY_NEVER_RETAIN';\n16\tlet root: string, bin: string, deploy: string;\n17\t\n18\tfunction baseline(path: string) {\n19\t  const result = spawnSync('git', ['show', `${base}:${path}`], { encoding: 'utf8' });\n20\t  if (result.status !== 0) throw new Error(result.stderr);\n21\t  return result.stdout;\n22\t}\n23\t\n24\tfunction validator(source: string) {\n25\t  const marker = \"          if ! jq -e --arg source \\\"$GITHUB_SHA\\\" '\\n\";\n26\t  const start = source.indexOf(marker) + marker.length;\n27\t  const end = source.indexOf(\"          ' \\\"$work/inventory.json\\\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\", start);\n28\t  if (start < marker.length || end < start) throw new Error('missing real host validator');\n29\t  return { filter: source.slice(start, end), outside: `${source.slice(0, start)}<FILTER>${source.slice(end)}` };\n30\t}\n31\t\n32\tfunction gate(body: unknown) {\n33\t  return spawnSync('jq', ['-e', '--arg', 'source', sha, validator(workflow).filter], {\n34\t    input: JSON.stringify(body), encoding: 'utf8', env: { PATH: '/usr/bin:/bin', NODE_ENV: 'test' }\n35\t  });\n36\t}\n37\t\n38\tfunction tool(name: string, body: string) {\n39\t  const path = join(bin, name);\n40\t  writeFileSync(path, `#!${process.execPath}\\nconst fs=require('node:fs'),a=process.argv.slice(2),e=process.env;\\nfs.appendFileSync(e.CALLS,JSON.stringify([${JSON.stringify(name)},...a])+'\\\\n');\\n${body}\\n`);\n41\t  chmodSync(path, 0o755);\n42\t}\n43\t\n44\tfunction snapshot(directory = deploy): unknown {\n45\t  return readdirSync(directory).sort().map((name) => {\n46\t    const path = join(directory, name), stat = statSync(path);\n47\t    return [name, stat.mode, stat.isDirectory() ? snapshot(path) : readFileSync(path).toString('hex')];\n48\t  });\n49\t}\n50\t\n51\tfunction calls(): string[][] {\n52\t  const path = join(root, 'calls');\n53\t  return existsSync(path) ? readFileSync(path, 'utf8').trim().split('\\n').map((line) => JSON.parse(line)) : [];\n54\t}\n55\t\n56\ttype Probe = { status: string; pipeline_exit_status: number | null; captured_bytes: number | null; home_present: boolean };\n57\tfunction run(options: { output?: string; code?: number; pipelineCode?: number; headCode?: number; hang?: boolean; home?: string; early?: string; args?: string[]; source?: string; validate?: boolean } = {}) {\n58\t  const env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv = {\n59\t    NODE_ENV: 'test',\n60\t    PATH: `${bin}:/usr/bin:/bin`, CALLS: join(root, 'calls'), LC_ALL: 'en_US.UTF-8',\n61\t    OUTPUT: Buffer.from(options.output ?? 'v2.35.1\\n').toString('base64'), CODE: String(options.code ?? 0),\n62\t    PIPELINE_CODE: options.pipelineCode === undefined ? '' : String(options.pipelineCode),\n63\t    HEAD_CODE: options.headCode === undefined ? '' : String(options.headCode),\n64\t    HANG: options.hang ? '1' : '', EARLY: options.early ?? '', CANARY: secret\n65\t  };\n66\t  if (options.home !== undefined) env.HOME = options.home;\n67\t  const before = snapshot();\n68\t  const result = spawnSync('/bin/bash', [options.source ?? join(process.cwd(), scriptPath), ...(options.args ?? [deploy, sha])], {\n69\t    env, encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 10_000\n70\t  });\n71\t  expect(result.error).toBeUndefined();\n72\t  expect(result.stdout + result.stderr).not.toContain(secret);\n73\t  expect(result.stdout + result.stderr).not.toContain(homeCanary);\n74\t  expect(result.stderr).toBe('');\n75\t  expect(snapshot()).toEqual(before);\n76\t  const body = JSON.parse(result.stdout);\n77\t  if (options.validate !== false) expect(gate(body).status, JSON.stringify(body)).toBe(0);\n78\t  return { result, body, probe: body.compose_probe as Probe, calls: calls() };\n79\t}\n80\t\n81\tfunction expectComposeRefusal(value: ReturnType<typeof run>, probe: Probe) {\n82\t  expect(value.result.status).toBe(1);\n83\t  expect(value.body).toMatchObject({ outcome: 'refused', reason: 'compose_unavailable', versions: { compose: 'unknown' } });\n84\t  expect(value.probe).toEqual(probe);\n85\t  expect(value.calls.filter(([name]) => name === 'timeout')).toEqual([\n86\t    ['timeout', '--signal=KILL', '5s', 'uname', '-s'],\n87\t    ['timeout', '--signal=KILL', '5s', 'uname', '-m'],\n88\t    ['timeout', '--signal=KILL', '5s', 'df', '-Pk', '--', deploy],\n89\t    ['timeout', '--signal=KILL', '5s', 'docker', 'version', '--format', '{{.Server.Version}}'],\n90\t    ['timeout', '--signal=KILL', '5s', 'docker', 'compose', 'version', '--short']\n91\t  ]);\n92\t  expect(value.calls.filter(([name]) => name === 'docker')).toEqual([\n93\t    ['docker', 'version', '--format', '{{.Server.Version}}'], ['docker', 'compose', 'version', '--short']\n94\t  ]);\n95\t  expect(value.calls.filter(([name]) => name === 'head')).toEqual(Array.from({ length: 5 }, () => ['head', '-c', '16385']));\n96\t  expect(value.calls.some(([name]) => ['stat', 'sha256sum', 'curl'].includes(name))).toBe(false);\n97\t  expect(value.body.files).toEqual({});\n98\t}\n99\t\n100\tdescribe.skipIf(process.platform === 'win32')('fixed Compose-only preflight observability', () => {\n101\t  beforeEach(() => {\n102\t    root = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'hpo-')); bin = join(root, 'bin'); deploy = join(root, 'deploy');\n103\t    mkdirSync(bin); mkdirSync(deploy);\n104\t    writeFileSync(join(deploy, '.env'), `AUTH_SECRET=${secret}\\n`);\n105\t    writeFileSync(join(deploy, 'docker-compose.yml'), `# ${secret}\\nservices: {}\\n`);\n106\t    tool('timeout', `const {spawnSync}=require('node:child_process');\n107\t      if(a.shift()!=='--signal=KILL'||a.shift()!=='5s')process.exit(99);\n108\t      const command=a.shift(),r=spawnSync(command,a,{timeout:5000,killSignal:'SIGKILL'});\n109\t      const code=command==='docker'&&a[0]==='compose'&&e.PIPELINE_CODE!==''?Number(e.PIPELINE_CODE):r.error?.code==='ETIMEDOUT'?124:r.status??1;\n110\t      if(r.stderr)process.stderr.write(r.stderr);\n111\t      process.stdout.on('error',()=>process.exit(code));\n112\t      process.stdout.write(r.stdout||Buffer.alloc(0),()=>process.exit(code));`);\n113\t    tool('head', `const {spawnSync}=require('node:child_process');\n114\t      const input=fs.readFileSync(0),r=spawnSync('/usr/bin/head',a,{input});\n115\t      const code=e.HEAD_CODE!==''&&input.equals(Buffer.from(e.OUTPUT,'base64'))?Number(e.HEAD_CODE):r.status??1;\n116\t      process.stdout.write(r.stdout);process.exit(code);`);\n117\t    tool('uname', `if(e.EARLY==='platform')process.exit(4);console.log(a[0]==='-s'?'Linux':'x86_64');`);\n118\t    tool('df', `console.log(e.EARLY==='space'?'invalid':'Filesystem 1024-blocks Used Available Capacity Mounted on\\\\nfixture 100000 100 99900 1% /scope');`);\n119\t    tool('stat', `const s=fs.statSync(a.at(-1));console.log(a[1]==='%s'?s.size:(s.mode&0o7777).toString(8));`);\n120\t    tool('sha256sum', `console.log(require('node:crypto').createHash('sha256').update(fs.readFileSync(a.at(-1))).digest('hex')+'  fixture');`);\n121\t    tool('curl', `process.exit(99);`);\n122\t    tool('docker', `process.stderr.write(e.CANARY);\n123\t      if(a[0]==='version'){if(e.EARLY==='docker')process.exit(3);console.log('29.1.3');return;}\n124\t      if(JSON.stringify(a)===JSON.stringify(['compose','version','--short'])){\n125\t        if(e.HANG){setTimeout(()=>process.exit(0),60000);return;}\n126\t        process.stdout.write(Buffer.from(e.OUTPUT,'base64'),()=>process.exit(Number(e.CODE)));return;\n127\t      }\n128\t      if(a[0]==='ps')return;\n129\t      process.exit(99);`);\n130\t  });\n131\t  afterEach(() => rmSync(root, { recursive: true, force: true }));\n132\t\n133\t  it.each([undefined, '', homeCanary])('records HOME presence only, including empty HOME %#', (home) => {\n134\t    const value = run({ home, output: 'v2.35.1\\n\\n\\n' });\n135\t    expect(value.probe).toEqual({ status: 'ok', pipeline_exit_status: 0, captured_bytes: 7, home_present: home !== undefined });\n136\t    expect(value.body.versions.compose).toBe('v2.35.1');\n137\t    expect(value.body.reason).toBe('missing_or_multiple_app');\n138\t    expect(value.calls.filter(([name]) => name === 'docker').at(-1)).toEqual([\n139\t      'docker', 'ps', '-a', '--filter', 'label=com.docker.compose.project=tokenizer', '--filter', 'label=com.docker.compose.service=app', '--format', '{{.ID}}'\n140\t    ]);\n141\t  });\n142\t\n143\t  it.each([1, 23, 124, 137, 141, 255])('retains whole bounded pipeline status %i without cause inference', (code) => {\n144\t    expectComposeRefusal(run({ pipelineCode: code, output: `${secret}\\n\\n` }), {\n145\t      status: 'command_failed', pipeline_exit_status: code, captured_bytes: Buffer.byteLength(secret), home_present: false\n146\t    });\n147\t  });\n148\t\n149\t  it('records command failure even when stdout is valid semver', () => {\n150\t    expectComposeRefusal(run({ code: 7, output: '2.35.1\\n' }), {\n151\t      status: 'command_failed', pipeline_exit_status: 7, captured_bytes: 6, home_present: false\n152\t    });\n153\t  });\n154\t\n155\t  it('records the rightmost failing capture stage, not necessarily the Docker exit code', () => {\n156\t    expectComposeRefusal(run({ code: 7, headCode: 141, output: 'v2.35.1\\n' }), {\n157\t      stat